# THM-2904 -- all-root finite ranked-H1 Hunter closure and 121 new j=6 roots

**PROVED + FINITE-EXACT + VERIFIED.**

## 1. Exact marked-suffix universe

Use the `41,415` marked gate branches of THM-2899.  On each of its
`14,806` scalar-hard branches retain the literal data

```text
E, gate rank j, apex a_j, excluded prefix P_j,
C=G_E minus D_(a_j), h=|C|, and components(C).
```

Let

```text
q_1>=...>=q_5
```

be the globally sealed allowed singleton coverages on `C`, and put

```text
R_4=q_1+q_2+q_3+q_4.
```

Exactly `6,180` hard branches satisfy

```text
R_4<6h/7.                                                   (1)
```

For such a branch, THM-2897 makes `R_4` a valid four-set complement cap.
THM-2893 with `(k,s)=(5,1)` therefore forces all five labels of a
hypothetical cover into

```text
H_1={w>=15:w notin P_j and c_C(w)>=h-R_4}.                 (2)
```

Put

```text
epsilon=6h/7-R_4>0,
N=ceil((99/70) components(C)/(7 epsilon))-1.               (3)
```

The strict THM-735(ii) discrepancy estimate proves that every member of
`H_1` is at most `N`.  Thus scanning every allowed `15<=w<=N` computes the
whole core; no finite-window proposal is used as a global statement.

This theorem takes the exact finite stratum

```text
N<=15000.                                                   (4)
```

It contains `5,999` branches.  The other `181` rows satisfying `(1)` lie
outside the theorem's route and remain explicitly deferred.

## 2. Ordered Hunter stars

Order each exact core

```text
H_1=(x_1,...,x_t)
```

by decreasing `c_C`, breaking ties by speed.  Any five-set in `H_1` has a
unique earliest member `x_i`; its other four labels lie in the exact later
core suffix.  Put

```text
C_i=C minus D_(x_i).
```

If the four largest exact child coverages

```text
|C_i intersect D_y|,             y in {x_(i+1),...,x_t},
```

sum to less than `|C_i|`, subadditivity closes every five-set assigned to
`x_i`.  The implementation first tries the inherited upper bounds
`c_C(y)` on that same suffix, and computes exact child coverages only when
needed.  It never reintroduces labels outside the later `H_1` suffix.

This is exactly THM-2893's ordered high-core pivot.  In THM-2897's
relative-Hunter language it is the spanning-tree star at `x_i`: if

```text
i(x,y)=|C intersect D_x intersect D_y|,
S(Q)=sum_(v in Q)c_C(v),
sigma_x(Q)=sum_(y in Q minus {x})i(x,y),
```

then the pivot invoice is

```text
S(Q)-sigma_x(Q)
 =c_C(x)+sum_(y in Q minus {x})|C_x intersect D_y|.        (5)
```

The exact ordered-star test closes `5,975` of the `5,999` finite branches.
Their core sizes and raw five-set workloads reach

```text
|H_1|=444,                    binom(444,5)=140,578,526,088.
```

The nearest-rank core-size quantiles are

```text
percent      0  25  50  75  90  95  99  100
|H_1|        5   8  16  36  83 141 283  444.              (6)
```

The smallest positive star/local margin is `1/3166020`.

## 3. Nonstar Hunter repair

Exactly `24` branches have a star-open pivot.  On every one it is the
first core vertex, and there is no other open pivot.  A star-invoice
branch-and-bound leaves only `54` hostile five-sets in total, between one
and ten per branch.

For each such five-set `Q`, compute the exact complete overlap graph and
the maximum spanning-tree credit

```text
tau_5(Q)=max_T sum_({x,y} in T)i(x,y),
psi_5(Q)=S(Q)-tau_5(Q).                                    (7)
```

Every one of the `54` sets satisfies

```text
psi_5(Q)<h.                                                 (8)
```

The minimum strict margin in `(8)` is

```text
1799771/75716368
```

at

```text
E=(1,2,4,6,10,11,13), gate rank 4.
```

Thus all `24` star survivors close by a genuinely nonstar Hunter tree.
The independent exact residual branch-and-bound also closes them, but is
not needed in the theorem mechanism.  Consequently

```text
5975 star closures + 24 nonstar-tree closures = 5999.       (9)
```

No witness occurs.

## 4. Whole-root consequence

For exactly `132` seven-body roots, every scalar-hard marked branch belongs
to the finite closed stratum `(9)`; all other gate branches close by
THM-2899's scalar test.  The ordered THM-2896 gate therefore excludes every
external six-label cover on each of these roots.  THM-2892 closes the
eight-body chamber when an added label lies in `{1,...,14} minus E`.
Hence all `132` roots are proved.

The locked output lists all `132` roots and has root-set digest

```text
c5eb5a86bbe82c2dc46113527e67f6a1f50add87b100cad916ee6367d7177a13.
```

The official proved union before this theorem has `17` roots, including
THM-2902's two omission-six roots.  Eleven of those `17` occur in the
displayed `132`; the exact set difference has

```text
132-11=121
```

new roots and digest

```text
3b133f35fa91191819b35a2760dcdf822cf8523818776584b02de36939658b47.
```

The resulting official union and residual are

```text
proved roots = 17+121 = 138,
remaining roots = 3432-138 = 3294.                         (10)
```

The proved-union digest is

```text
8536e577993aa395a6d2e676ea2c6ea0b29b99d1d15787dee4c7480fa0eebffa.
```

No provisional later root claim is included in this comparison.

## 5. Verification

The core verifier reconstructs every literal carrier directly, compares it
with apex subtraction, excludes the actual prefix, computes every exact
core label through `(3)`, checks strict inequalities, and directly
reconstructs any returned witness.  Thirty-two deterministic shards cover
the exact ordered body atlas once.  The locked merge verifies all shard
hashes, counts, the exact `132`-root list, the `121`-root set difference,
and the official union.

Exact aggregate:

```text
roots                                  3432
marked gate branches                  41415
scalar-hard branches                  14806
rank-four H1 eligible                  6180
finite N<=15000 branches               5999
closed                                 5999
witnesses                                 0
deferred cutoff branches                181
whole roots closed                       132.              (11)
```

The shard-file digest is

```text
d686d1afd01b494ca6aa9a4733816c774f7e8e4ed398081f556c44e4af7869a0,
```

and the aggregate semantic shard-ledger digest is

```text
f02aea1d70f89b2c634b84b313da9bba78b26718e85fe1731dbb9ef496559a9b.
```

The all-survivor Hunter semantic digest is

```text
030c5af7cdb8fe5c2c8188b3debb78e8e0aabb79a7e553308d0f11a411ded74b.
```

The locked merge and Hunter survivor audit have byte-identical ordinary
and optimized outputs and use explicit guards rather than Python
`assert`.  The full core shards likewise have no assertions; their
ordinary/optimized byte-parity audit is recorded in the result artifact.

## 6. Scope

This theorem closes exactly the finite rank-four route `(4)` and the `132`
whole roots certified by it.  It does not close or classify the `181`
eligible branches with `N>15000`, close the remaining `3294` roots, or
prove LRC(14).  A failure of `(1)` or `(4)` is not evidence for a cover.
The literal carrier, excluded gate prefix, later-core suffix, and
maximum-tree edge credits are theorem-bearing data and are not replaced by
unmarked residuals or scalar summaries.
